{"status":"ok","message-type":"work","message-version":"1.0.0","message":{"indexed":{"date-parts":[[2026,9,20]],"date-time":"2026-09-20T14:00:52Z","timestamp":1789912852723,"version":"4.0.1"},"reference-count":34,"publisher":"American Association for the Advancement of Science (AAAS)","issue":"5643","content-domain":{"domain":[],"crossmark-restriction":false},"short-container-title":["Science"],"published-print":{"date-parts":[[2003,10,10]]},"abstract":"<jats:p>\n                    Cell division in many mammalian tissues is associated with specific times of day, but just how the circadian clock controls this timing has not been clear. Here, we show in the regenerating liver (of mice) that the circadian clock controls the expression of cell cycle\u2013related genes that in turn modulate the expression of active Cyclin B1-Cdc2 kinase, a key regulator of mitosis. Among these genes, expression of\n                    <jats:italic>wee1<\/jats:italic>\n                    was directly regulated by the molecular components of the circadian clockwork. In contrast, the circadian clockwork oscillated independently of the cell cycle in single cells. Thus, the intracellular circadian clockwork can control the cell-division cycle directly and unidirectionally in proliferating cells.\n                  <\/jats:p>","DOI":"10.1126\/science.1086271","type":"journal-article","created":{"date-parts":[[2003,8,25]],"date-time":"2003-08-25T20:38:55Z","timestamp":1061843935000},"page":"255-259","source":"Crossref","is-referenced-by-count":962,"title":["Control Mechanism of the Circadian Clock for Timing of Cell Division in Vivo"],"prefix":"10.1126","volume":"302","author":[{"given":"Takuya","family":"Matsuo","sequence":"first","affiliation":[{"name":"Division of Molecular Brain Science, Department of Brain Sciences, Kobe University Graduate School of Medicine, Chuo-ku, Kobe 650\u20130017, Japan."},{"name":"Department of Physics, Informatics and Biology, Yamaguchi University, Yamaguchi 753\u20138512, Japan."}],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]},{"given":"Shun","family":"Yamaguchi","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"Division of Molecular Brain Science, Department of Brain Sciences, Kobe University Graduate School of Medicine, Chuo-ku, Kobe 650\u20130017, Japan."},{"name":"Department of Physics, Informatics and Biology, Yamaguchi University, Yamaguchi 753\u20138512, Japan."}],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]},{"given":"Shigeru","family":"Mitsui","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"Division of Molecular Brain Science, Department of Brain Sciences, Kobe University Graduate School of Medicine, Chuo-ku, Kobe 650\u20130017, Japan."},{"name":"Department of Physics, Informatics and Biology, Yamaguchi University, Yamaguchi 753\u20138512, Japan."}],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]},{"given":"Aki","family":"Emi","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"Division of Molecular Brain Science, Department of Brain Sciences, Kobe University Graduate School of Medicine, Chuo-ku, Kobe 650\u20130017, Japan."},{"name":"Department of Physics, Informatics and Biology, Yamaguchi University, Yamaguchi 753\u20138512, Japan."}],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]},{"given":"Fukuko","family":"Shimoda","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"Division of Molecular Brain Science, Department of Brain Sciences, Kobe University Graduate School of Medicine, Chuo-ku, Kobe 650\u20130017, Japan."},{"name":"Department of Physics, Informatics and Biology, Yamaguchi University, Yamaguchi 753\u20138512, Japan."}],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]},{"given":"Hitoshi","family":"Okamura","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"Division of Molecular Brain Science, Department of Brain Sciences, Kobe University Graduate School of Medicine, Chuo-ku, Kobe 650\u20130017, Japan."},{"name":"Department of Physics, Informatics and Biology, Yamaguchi University, Yamaguchi 753\u20138512, Japan."}],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]}],"member":"221","reference":[{"key":"e_1_3_2_2_2","first-page":"193","volume":"4","year":"2000","unstructured":"G. A. Bjarnason, R. Jordan, Prog. Cell Cycle Res.4, 193 (2000).","journal-title":"Prog. Cell Cycle Res."},{"key":"e_1_3_2_3_2","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1006\/cbir.2000.0585"},{"key":"e_1_3_2_4_2","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1002\/aja.1001680405"},{"key":"e_1_3_2_5_2","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1016\/0016-5085(91)90019-H"},{"key":"e_1_3_2_6_2","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1111\/1523-1747.ep12480379"},{"key":"e_1_3_2_7_2","first-page":"241","volume":"2","year":"1996","unstructured":"R. Smaaland, Prog. Cell Cycle Res.2, 241 (1996).","journal-title":"Prog. Cell Cycle Res."},{"key":"e_1_3_2_8_2","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1159\/000144249"},{"key":"e_1_3_2_9_2","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1002\/ar.1091200408"},{"key":"e_1_3_2_10_2","first-page":"134","volume":"15","year":"1957","unstructured":"C. P. Barnum, C. D. Jardetsky, F. Halberg, Tex. Rep. Biol. Med.15, 134 (1957).","journal-title":"Tex. Rep. Biol. Med."},{"key":"e_1_3_2_11_2","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1016\/0014-4827(66)90484-8"},{"key":"e_1_3_2_12_2","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.3109\/07420528509055556"},{"key":"e_1_3_2_13_2","first-page":"539","volume":"9","year":"1995","unstructured":"H. Barbason et al., In Vivo9, 539 (1995).","journal-title":"In Vivo"},{"key":"e_1_3_2_14_2","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1126\/science.172.3984.738"},{"key":"e_1_3_2_15_2","first-page":"186","volume":"12","year":"1931","unstructured":"G. M. Higgins, R. M. Anderson, Arch. Pathol.12, 186 (1931).","journal-title":"Arch. Pathol."},{"key":"e_1_3_2_16_2","unstructured":"Materials and methods are available as supporting material on Science Online."},{"key":"e_1_3_2_17_2","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1016\/S0955-0674(99)80036-2"},{"key"